{"path":"locale/messages/close","title":"std::messages<CharT>::close, std::messages<CharT>::do_close","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::messages&lt;CharT&gt;::</span>close, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::messages&lt;CharT&gt;::</span>do_close","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/locale/messages/close","section":"locale","kind":"page","summary":"On POSIX systems, this function call usually translates to a call to catclose(). In GNU libstdc++, which is implemented in terms of GNU gettext(), it does nothing.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/locale\">&lt;locale&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">public</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> close<span class=\"br0\">(</span> catalog c <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> do_close<span class=\"br0\">(</span> catalog c <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Public member function, calls the protected virtual member function <code>do_close</code> of the most derived class.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Releases the implementation-defined resources associated with an open catalog that is designated by the value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">c</span></code> of type <code>catalog</code> (inherited from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/messages_base\">std::messages_base</a></span>), which was obtained from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/messages/open\">open()</a></span>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> c\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a valid open catalog identifier, on which <code>close()</code> has not yet been called\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>On POSIX systems, this function call usually translates to a call to <code><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/catclose.html\" data-external=\"1\">catclose()</a></code>. In GNU libstdc++, which is implemented in terms of GNU <code>gettext()</code>, it does nothing. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The following example demonstrated retrieval of messages: on a typical GNU/Linux system it reads from <code>/usr/share/locale/de/LC_MESSAGES/sed.mo</code>.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;locale&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale\"><span class=\"kw1911\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span></span></a> loc<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"de_DE.utf8\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">imbue</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>loc<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> facet <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/use_facet\"><span class=\"kw1914\">std::<span class=\"me2\">use_facet</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/messages\"><span class=\"kw1963\">std::<span class=\"me2\">messages</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>loc<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> cat <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> facet.<span class=\"me1\">open</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"sed\"</span>, loc<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>cat <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Could not open german <span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span>sed<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span> message catalog<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span>No match<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span> in German: \"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> facet.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>cat, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"No match\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span>Memory exhausted<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span> in German: \"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> facet.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>cat, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"st0\">\"Memory exhausted\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    facet.<span class=\"me1\">close</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>cat<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>\"No match\" in German: Keine Übereinstimmung\n\"Memory exhausted\" in German: Speicher erschöpft</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr><td></td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"locale","title":"Localization library"},{"path":"locale/messages","title":"std::messages"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::messages<CharT>::close, std::messages<CharT>::do_close","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Public member function, calls the protected virtual member function do_close of the most derived class."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"c"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"On POSIX systems, this function call usually translates to a call to catclose()."},{"label":"Example","note":"The following example demonstrated retrieval of messages: on a typical GNU/Linux system it reads from /usr/share/locale/de/LC_MESSAGES/sed.mo."},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":207,"codeBlockCount":2}
